2. The respondents have filed the reply. Respondents contend that thecomplainants are the investors and they are not allottees because in Para 11& 18 of the provisional allotment letters they have admitted that they areinvestors. The provisional letters for booking are subject to approvals andpermissions to be granted by various authorities for construction. It is acontingent contract and therefore it cannot be enforced as the approvals andpermissions required for construction have not been granted. Section 18 ofRERA is not retrospective. Hence they request to dismiss the complaints.3. Following points arise for my determination and findings thereof areas under:
Points.1. \Alhether the respondents failed tocomplete the project as agreed?
2. Whether the complainants are entitledto get back their amount with interest?
Findings.Affirmative.
Affirmative
Reasons.4. In Neelkamal Realtors Suburban Pvt. Ltd. - v/s- Union of India(W.P.No. 2737 of 2017) Their Lordships of Bombay High court have heldthat sections '1,2 and 18 of RERA are retroactive. A1lotment letters disclosethe fact that the complainants agreed to purchase and respondents agreedto sell flats and therefore I do not find that complainants are investors. I findthat they are allottees as defined by section 2(d) of RERA, hence thisAuthority has jurisdiction to entertain these complaints5. Complainants have relied upon the allotment letters issued by therespondents. on their perusal it becomes clear that the respondents made
3

